From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devin <devin@cognition.ai>
Date: Sun, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: give the Pages deploy its own BASE_PATH-scoped build

cd.yml's Pages job deployed the shared `production-build` artifact —
built with vite base '/', so every hashed asset URL in index.html
resolved to the domain root and 404'd on
https://<owner>.github.io/Qui-Browser/ (blank page). The same artifact
also feeds Netlify, which correctly wants base '/', so the Pages job
now builds its own dist with BASE_PATH=/Qui-Browser/ (the identical
fix patch 0003 made in deploy.yml).

---
diff --git a/.github/workflows/cd.yml b/.github/workflows/cd.yml
index 055fc1e..3f090af 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/cd.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/cd.yml
@@ -87,11 +87,26 @@ jobs:
       url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}
 
     steps:
-      - name: Download build artifacts
-        uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
+      - name: Checkout code
+        uses: actions/checkout@v4
+
+      - name: Setup Node.js
+        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
         with:
-          name: production-build
-          path: dist
+          node-version: ${{ env.NODE_VERSION }}
+          cache: 'npm'
+
+      - name: Install dependencies
+        run: npm ci
+
+      # Pages serves this repo under /Qui-Browser/, so this target needs its own
+      # build — the shared `production-build` artifact is emitted with base '/'
+      # (correct for Netlify's root deploy) and would 404 every asset here.
+      - name: Build for GitHub Pages
+        run: npm run build
+        env:
+          NODE_ENV: production
+          BASE_PATH: /Qui-Browser/
 
       - name: Setup Pages
         uses: actions/configure-pages@v3
